														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4851304">
									

<p>Basically a brainstorming thread for a potential SCP.</p>
<p>The idea behind it involves an SCP that, in its present state at the time of the article, is a tank of amber-colored water. In a solid or liquid state, the water has no special properties other than its unusual color. In a gaseous state, however - particularly a semi-gaseous mist - the water transports whomever travels through it to an oceanic world with no fauna.</p>
<p>Despite this, I'm thinking that the world is very friendly to life - the seas are freshwater, and there's a diverse ecosystem of plant life beneath the surface, some of which are edible and moderately nutritious to humans, despite their alien nature.</p>
<p>The SCP story itself involves an SCP scientist who's sent to investigate the unusual amber cloud hovering about a mile off the coast of Tanzania, when a powerful wind blows it into him before he has time to adjust his course, transporting him to the oceanic world, where he encounters a large sentient cetacean-like creature and a sentient, flying arachnid-like creature. The story itself would explore the backstory of the world, and the interactions of three sentient creatures and how they interact with their environment when they're unequally built for it, and the power dynamic that emerges as a result of their unequal adaptations.</p>
<p>I'm still figuring out the mechanics behind the mist itself, though the fact that it only facilitates transportation as a mist and not in any other state of matter is key to the story's resolution.</p>

